# End-to-end evidence

Machina Practica evidence contract: 1.0.1
Profile: web-playwright
Project adaptations: record chosen viewports, actors, local fixtures and scope.
Canonical baseline environment: record the pinned OS/browser/font environment and reviewer.

## Observable outcome

Describe what the blank shell actually exposes and how source identity is visible. List unimplemented product behavior plainly. Link each scenario to its ordinary action and semantic outcome; generate its walkthrough from completed step receipts.

## Run and retain

Document the one verifier command, production server command, bounded startup check, fixed clocks/seeds, bundled assets, network allowlist and per-worker storage. Link actual logs, traces, capture receipts and source/artifact hashes. Capture candidates after semantics and presentation readiness. A failed test retains partial evidence and remains failed.

## Wait-policy enforcement

Name the verifier stage that rejects `waitForTimeout` references in browser-test source, and retain a negative fixture showing that it fails. Use the supplied AST checker or an equivalent linter. Review other timers and readiness conditions in context. A deadline can bound a wait; a fixed delay cannot prove readiness or that a delayed response was handled. Font or raster settling is not an exception.

## Review and delivery

Define the candidate review record (hash, source, platform, reviewer), required exact-pixel comparisons, and cross-platform limits. CI must retain failure artifacts. A trusted preview publisher must validate repository/PR/run/head/artifact identity and never execute untrusted artifact code or overwrite production/unrelated previews. State external delivery that has actually been verified.

## Limits

List untested browsers, native/hardware behavior, external credentials and production-only services. Local fixtures prove only the scenarios executed. Never infer baseline approval from a generated screenshot or deployment from a green build.
